            <p>Aspergilloma Mass. An axial computed tomography (CT) scan of the lung demonstrates a round, enhancing lesion with a surrounding air shadow in the superior basal segment of the right lower lobe, measuring 2.5 cm &#x000d7; 1.6 cm. This finding is characteristic of the Monod sign and indicates the presence of an aspergilloma. Contributed by S Sarkar, MD, and B Ghewade, MD</p>
