      <floats-group id="article-17891.s17">
        <fig id="article-17891.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>HRCT Chest Scan Showing Aspergilloma With SARS-CoV-2 Pneumonitis Features. A high-resolution computed tomography (HRCT) scan of the chest reveals bilateral peripheral ground-glass opacities and a right upper lobe cavity measuring 2.3 &#x000d7; 2.3 cm and containing an opacity, likely a fungal ball. These findings are consistent with SARS-CoV-2 pneumonitis and indicate an aspergilloma. Chaurasia S, Thimmappa M, Chowdhury S. Case report: chronic cavitatory pulmonary aspergillosis after COVID-19. <italic toggle="yes">Am J Trop Med Hyg.</italic> 2021;106(1):105-107. doi: 10.4269/ajtmh.21-0701.&#x000a0;</p>
          </caption>
